# D-fast: Deribit BTC perpetual moves >= 1 bp in 0.3 s -> buy that side at the ask, sell at the bid 12 s later.
# Live from 25 Oct 07:15 UTC ($10 a trade; $5 = 5 shares from 08:05 after a 6-trade test lost $5). From Stockholm Deribit showed BTC moves before Binance futures on 88% of 80 moves (median
# +111 ms); first hour on paper +3.8 c/share vs Binance -3.6 (feedrace.py, racesim.py). Loaded after realistic.env.
BN_SOURCE=deribit
BN_SOCKETS=1
TK_MOVE_BPS=1
TK_MOVE_SEC=0.3
TK_HOLD=12
TK_SIZE=5
TK_MAX_TRADE_USD=5
TK_MAX_DAY_LOSS=15
# D-HY exit (TK_HOLD_IF_UP=1) was live 09:43-10:25 UTC 25 Oct and reverted: 4 trades -$2.32 (held a 0.55 bid, lost
# -$1.93); held positions also escape the daily loss cap and mix shares in one token (code review). Back to the plain
# 12 s scalp, which made +$3.99 over 41 live trades at $5 (08:04-09:43).
